  "description": "Why do you feel drained after socializing, even when you had a great time? Researchers at the University of Helsinki checked in on people five times a day for 12 days. Being sociable lifted their mood in the moment, but they felt more tired about three hours later, extroverts included. Here's what that means for your social battery.\n\nFollow The Human Side for more on the things we feel but rarely talk about.",
